summary:
  The media key's Pause stops an episode or a My Music file as it stops a
  station, and keeps nothing of it.

history:
  Up to 2026.43 a pause was a stop for anything without a timeshift buffer.
  The stop threw the episode away, and the next Play, which names nothing,
  put the first station of the list on. Measured 2026-11-11 on main.qml's own
  functions around a counting player: Pause left the source and the episode
  key empty, and two presses of the widget's button ended in "radio:0".
  2026.44 answers "keep" for a file that plays here: it pauses where it
  stands, and Play goes on from there.

target:
  package/contents/ui/TransportLogic.js

find:
          if (here) return ownFile === true ? "keep" : "pause";

replace:
          if (here) return "pause";

expect:
  Killed by tests/qml/tst_transportlogic.qml::test_a_pause_keeps_the_episode_or_the_file_that_plays
  and tests/qml/tst_transportroads.qml::test_play_after_the_pause_goes_on_in_place.
  Line-neutral.
